        <mxCell id="t2" value="vxedge — next-generation SDV zonal E/E architecture · software perspective" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=30;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#263238;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="100" y="100" width="1700" height="46" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t2s" value="Same six zones as the hardware page, read as a layered software stack. Columns align 1:1 with the hardware zones; bands are layers. The control plane (right) is API-first: vxedged owns all orchestration behind vxAPI (gRPC/Protobuf); every frontend is a thin client. Manifests (YAML) and vxAPI (Protobuf) are the only two cross-language interfaces — ARCHITECTURE.md §4, §5." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=13;fontColor=#546E7A;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="100" y="152" width="1760" height="46" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
